WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.220
(audience applauding)

00:00:01.220 --> 00:00:02.800
- Thank you very, very much.

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:08.330
That was my grandson,

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:10.660
Halfdan, (chuckles) and I was

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:15.900
actually 13 years younger than him

00:00:18.427 --> 00:00:19.627
when I wanted to be part

00:00:21.547 --> 00:00:22.893
of the actors group.

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:27.600
I wanted to be an actress, and I went

00:00:28.715 --> 00:00:31.763
to the theater school in Norway,

00:00:34.029 --> 00:00:38.340
and I was going to show them
Juliet in Romeo and Juliet.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:39.770
I was 17 years old,

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:42.840
but I understood
everything about her story,

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.000
and she had just heard

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.990
that Romeo was dead,

00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:51.570
and now she wanted to take her life,

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:54.300
and she had a glass of poison.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.960
And the way I had studied it by myself,

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:58.850
I didn't speak much to other people,

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:01.850
but I did a lot on my own,

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:04.540
even my first theater thing,

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:06.370
and I came in front of the jury

00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:11.370
and I showed them what I
knew about someone's death.

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:14.060
It was a glass of poison,
and what I wanted,

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:16.630
it was to drink this glass

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:19.190
and think of Romeo, and then, slowly,

00:01:19.190 --> 00:01:23.130
I would fall down and
down and down on the floor

00:01:24.237 --> 00:01:25.070
and die.

00:01:27.239 --> 00:01:31.090
And then I heard from
the three jury people,

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:33.220
I heard the oldest of them say,

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:36.330
in the middle of me going
down and down and down,

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:38.850
she said, "Thank you, Liv
Ullmann, this is enough."

00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:42.605
(audience laughing loudly)

00:01:42.605 --> 00:01:45.250
I cried, and I couldn't understand it

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:48.840
because it was the one thing
I knew I could, it was acting.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:52.910
And I went home to my grandmother in Oslo

00:01:52.910 --> 00:01:55.160
and I rang the doorbell, and she opened,

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:57.860
and I said, (tearfully) "I didn't make it,

00:01:57.860 --> 00:02:00.380
and this is what I did, down and down,"

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:03.360
and she looked at me and she
said, "Oh, it's wonderful."

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:05.700
She didn't understand a word of it,

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:08.170
and then she took me

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:10.070
into her bed,

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:11.690
and we were to sleep,

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:14.710
and I was crying and she
put the blanket over us,

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:19.040
and there I was lying so close to her,

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:21.370
and I felt so safe, you know.

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:22.833
I felt this,

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:27.620
this breathing and everything in her neck.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:30.630
She smelled so well,

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:33.730
and I knew that I belonged,

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:35.460
and she was my best friend.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:38.450
From when I was 11, we went and saw films.

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:40.210
My whole upbringing

00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:44.010
was very often from films,
sitting in the quiet

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:48.080
of the theater and watching the Italians,

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:51.820
Miracolo a Milano, "Bicycle Thieves".

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:53.240
American movies,

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:56.030
I cried with Susan Hayward

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:57.940
and so many others.

00:02:57.940 --> 00:02:59.850
I watched them

00:02:59.850 --> 00:03:01.660
as a child.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:05.940
And the jury of my theater
school, where I didn't come in,

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:08.433
they would never believe
what happened to me,

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:12.880
because then a lot of
things happened to me.

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:14.520
As a matter of fact, in Norway,

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:17.830
sometimes, it is impossible to
have something happen to you

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:20.560
because everyone must be alike,

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:23.600
and you have to live by a certain rule,

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:26.450
don't brag, don't show
anything and whatever.

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:28.040
That's why I brought 20 people

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:30.036
from Norway here today. (laughs)

00:03:30.036 --> 00:03:33.578
(audience laughing and applauding)

00:03:33.578 --> 00:03:37.600
So (chuckles) they can tell Norway

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:41.810
it is true, she got an Oscar!
(audience laughing)

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:44.173
They are very important to me for that.

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:47.230
And I continued my career,

00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:49.420
I did a lot of stuff in Norway,

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:51.700
but coming out in the big world,

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:53.890
meeting new teachers all the time,

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:57.920
meeting teachers among
actors, among directors,

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:02.140
among so many things, meeting teachers,

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:03.180
teachers

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:08.820
that made me love to be
part of the painters,

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:11.250
the musicians,

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:12.880
the dancers.

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:16.170
Everything that is part of art,

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:18.000
I was one of them.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.540
Even Richard Rodgers,
you won't believe it,

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:22.590
he wrote a musical for me,

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:24.530
and I don't sing and I don't dance.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.998
He gave me seven songs on Broadway.

00:04:26.998 --> 00:04:29.970
(audience laughing)
(Liv chuckles)

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:32.470
I was so lucky,

00:04:32.470 --> 00:04:36.390
and then I got to do "Anna Christie",

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:40.930
and John, who I love, and I
haven't seen him for years,

00:04:40.930 --> 00:04:43.951
and, well.
(John chuckling)

00:04:43.951 --> 00:04:45.801
(audience applauding)

00:04:45.801 --> 00:04:48.218
(Liv laughs)

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:52.937
And it was incredible, and
I saw me and I thought,

00:04:52.937 --> 00:04:56.080
"Oh, they must know and
see this in Norway."

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:58.187
They had a magazine cover saying,

00:04:58.187 --> 00:05:01.110
"This is the new Nordic
star, Greta Garbo,"

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:04.000
and I was walking on Fifth Avenue,

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:08.510
and there Greta Garbo came,
and I was so full of myself,

00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:11.870
and I wanted to tell her, "I
am doing 'Anna Christie',"

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:14.000
and I went towards her, and she saw me,

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.100
and she got really scared

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:17.120
and she started to run.
(audience laughing)

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:20.880
And I had to run after her
because I had to tell who I was

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:22.930
and why I was and all of that,

00:05:22.930 --> 00:05:25.440
and she ran faster and looked at me,

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:27.357
and I ran very fast, too.
(audience laughing)

00:05:27.357 --> 00:05:29.860
(breathing heavily) And
we came to Central Park,

00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:34.140
and she looked terrified at
me and went into Central Park,

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:37.620
and I never saw her again.
(audience laughing)

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:41.850
And I suddenly, I suddenly
believed one thing,

00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:45.253
I was a little full of myself, you know?

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:48.730
I was seeing me,

00:05:48.730 --> 00:05:51.470
but I wasn't seeing the other person.

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:55.000
I wasn't recognizing the other person.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:58.660
And then, when I did this
musical with Richard Rodgers,

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:01.410
and I was to give away a lot of money

00:06:01.410 --> 00:06:05.450
because all the actors on
Broadway, they collected money,

00:06:05.450 --> 00:06:09.640
so we would help people
who were living in ward

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:11.200
and come with truckloads

00:06:12.231 --> 00:06:15.480
of medicals and doctors and nurses,

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:18.050
and all the theaters collected this money,

00:06:18.050 --> 00:06:20.610
and I was the one to give it to the head

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:25.180
of the International Rescue
Committee, Leo Cherne.

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:29.033
And I made the speech,
and I gave him the money,

00:06:30.109 --> 00:06:32.710
and then I asked, because
my mother brought me up

00:06:32.710 --> 00:06:35.720
to do that, "Is there
something else I can do,"

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:38.730
and he said, "Well, we are
going with this truckload

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:40.690
of medicines and doctors,

00:06:40.690 --> 00:06:43.517
and so do you want to come with us?"

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:47.410
And I said, "Well, how
long will that take,"

00:06:47.410 --> 00:06:50.940
and he said, "It's for
the rest of your life,"

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:53.171
and I went, and my life changed,

00:06:53.171 --> 00:06:57.360
this about seeing other people,
recognizing other people,

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:01.180
not only seeing yourself
and recognizing yourself

00:07:01.180 --> 00:07:04.840
and what life has given you.

00:07:04.840 --> 00:07:09.590
And I came to an island I
didn't know very much about,

00:07:09.590 --> 00:07:12.933
where there was a lot of
refugees from Vietnam, Macau,

00:07:14.992 --> 00:07:18.250
and I came there and I spoke with people.

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:20.960
And then there was a place in Macau,

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:23.950
where it said, "People with leprosy",

00:07:23.950 --> 00:07:26.340
and I wasn't going to go in there,

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:28.138
and then there was a priest,

00:07:28.138 --> 00:07:33.138
a Catholic priest, following
me, and he looked at me,

00:07:33.513 --> 00:07:35.020
and then I went in

00:07:35.020 --> 00:07:37.940
because he looked at me.
(audience laughing)

00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:39.770
I came on the inside,

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:44.210
and there on the ground
was lying an old woman,

00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:47.640
and she was crying like a baby,

00:07:47.640 --> 00:07:49.830
and she was so severed

00:07:51.310 --> 00:07:54.830
in her face and her arms,
and he looked at me,

00:07:54.830 --> 00:07:57.980
and I knew she's crying, I have to go down

00:07:59.243 --> 00:08:01.740
and take care of her,

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:03.340
and so I did it.

00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:06.380
And the moment I came close to her

00:08:07.493 --> 00:08:12.380
and was holding her and
lifting her up a little,

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:13.820
suddenly she stopped crying,

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:17.230
and then came this sound, (mimics sobbing)

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:18.640
like a little baby does

00:08:20.223 --> 00:08:22.123
when it stops crying,

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:25.483
and here, in the neck,

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:29.670
it was the same as my grandmother,

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:32.700
and I realized my grandmother is here.

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:34.483
My mother, my sister,

00:08:36.738 --> 00:08:39.550
everybody is here as well,

00:08:39.550 --> 00:08:42.730
and it was an incredible change

00:08:43.889 --> 00:08:46.890
in what I really believed life was.

00:08:46.890 --> 00:08:50.090
I know life is about
finding out who you are

00:08:51.041 --> 00:08:53.070
and why you are,

00:08:53.070 --> 00:08:55.960
and not so long after, I came to India,

00:08:55.960 --> 00:08:59.540
and there was sitting
a girl in an orphanage,

00:08:59.540 --> 00:09:02.980
and she was beautiful,
with long black hair,

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:04.910
and we were sitting on her bed

00:09:04.910 --> 00:09:07.620
and I did this a little on her hair,

00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:10.930
and she did this a little on my hair

00:09:10.930 --> 00:09:14.543
because it was longer
then and I was young then.

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:18.140
And suddenly, this little girl

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:21.100
takes off a ring

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:25.060
with a red glass stone,
and she gives it to me

00:09:25.060 --> 00:09:28.620
and puts it on my finger.

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:31.370
And I told this story to a Quaker

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:37.590
fundraising things, and they
started to make a fundraising

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:41.030
that this little girl had
organized, and of course,

00:09:41.030 --> 00:09:44.320
she does know about it,
but hundreds and thousands

00:09:44.320 --> 00:09:47.870
of dollars came in from
the Quakers and fundraising

00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:51.080
that went everywhere
because this little girl

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:54.640
gave the one wonderful
thing she had to me,

00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:56.853
who had everything,

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:04.350
and that's why I am so sure there is no

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:05.233
the other.

00:10:07.300 --> 00:10:12.300
Recognizing is not recognizing
yourself only, but you should

00:10:12.490 --> 00:10:16.260
recognize yourself only, I thought,

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:19.460
but it's, in reality, to recognize

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:21.473
other people,

00:10:22.550 --> 00:10:25.500
and I'm so grateful

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:26.510
for this.

00:10:26.510 --> 00:10:28.570
When I got this call

00:10:30.684 --> 00:10:33.390
and it was David, I call
him David, you know,

00:10:33.390 --> 00:10:34.710
because he's so gentle,

00:10:34.710 --> 00:10:37.313
I've said hello to him
many times since I came,

00:10:38.460 --> 00:10:40.963
and he explained why I got this,

00:10:42.650 --> 00:10:46.570
I'm so grateful, and that John
would come and give it away.

00:10:46.570 --> 00:10:49.030
It somehow makes a circle

00:10:49.030 --> 00:10:51.350
in my life, and my friends are here.

00:10:51.350 --> 00:10:53.720
They can tell the people in Norway

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:58.720
why I got it, and thank you.
(audience applauding)

